-- src:1015 | (1) This regulation provides for alternatives to the deductions that would otherwise be allowed under regulation 58.
-- src:1016 | (2) Instead of a deduction in respect of the actual expenses incurred in relation to the acquisition or use of a motor vehicle, the following deductions are allowed according to the mileage covered on journeys undertaken in the assessment period for the purposes of the trade, profession or vocation—
-- src:1017 | (a) in a car, van or other motor vehicle (apart from a motorcycle), 45 pence per mile for the first 833 miles and 25 pence per mile thereafter; and
-- src:1018 | (b) on a motorcycle, 24 pence per mile,
-- src:1019 | and, if the motor vehicle is a car . . . , the only deduction allowed for the acquisition or use of that vehicle is a deduction under this paragraph.
-- src:1020 | (3) Where a person carrying on a trade, profession or vocation incurs expenses in relation to the use of accommodation occupied as their home, instead of a deduction in respect of the actual expenses, a deduction is allowed according to the number of hours spent in the assessment period on income generating activities related to the trade, profession or vocation as follows—
-- src:1021 | (a) at least 25 hours but no more than 50 hours, £10;
-- src:1022 | (b) more than 50 hours but no more than 100 hours, £18;
-- src:1023 | (c) more than 100 hours, £26.
-- src:1024 | (4) Where premises which are used by a person mainly for the purposes of a trade, profession or vocation are also occupied by that person for their personal use, whether alone or with other persons, the deduction allowed for expenses in relation to those premises is the amount that would be allowed under regulation 58(1) if the premises were used wholly and exclusively for purposes of the trade, profession or vocation, but reduced by the following amount according to the number of persons occupying the premises for their personal use—
-- src:1025 | (a) £350 for one person;
-- src:1026 | (b) £500 for two persons;
-- src:1027 | (c) £650 for three or more persons.
@ref reg 58; reg 59 (src:1001-1027)
GIVEN claimed IS AN `Expenses claimed for a trade, profession or vocation in an assessment period`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 58 and 59 — the premises payments` claimed MEANS
    sum (map (GIVEN payment YIELD `reg 58 — the deduction allowed for a payment` payment)
             (filter (GIVEN payment YIELD payment's `kind of payment` EQUALS `use of premises used mainly for the trade, profession or vocation and also occupied for personal use`) (claimed's payments)))

-- src:1001 | 58 Permitted expenses
-- src:1002 | (1) The deductions allowed in the calculation of self-employed earnings are amounts paid in the assessment period in respect of—
-- src:1003 | (a) expenses that have been wholly and exclusively incurred for purposes of the trade, profession or vocation; or
-- src:1004 | (b) in the case of expenses that have been incurred for more than one purpose, an identifiable part or proportion that has been wholly and exclusively incurred for the purposes of the trade, profession or vocation,
-- src:1005 | excluding any expenses that were incurred unreasonably.
-- src:1006 | (2) Payments deducted under paragraph (1) may include value added tax.
-- src:1007 | (3) No deduction may be made for payments in respect of—
-- src:1008 | (a) expenditure on non-depreciating assets (including property, shares or other assets held for investment purposes);
-- src:1009 | (b) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:1010 | (c) repayment of capital . . . in relation to a loan taken out for the purposes of the trade, profession or vocation;
-- src:1011 | (d) expenses for business entertainment.
-- src:1012 | (3A) A deduction for a payment of interest in relation to a loan taken out for the purposes of the trade, profession or vocation may not exceed £41.
-- src:1013 | (4) This regulation is subject to regulation 59.
-- src:1014 | 59 Flat rate deductions for mileage and use of home and adjustment for personal use of business premises
-- src:1015 | (1) This regulation provides for alternatives to the deductions that would otherwise be allowed under regulation 58.
-- src:1016 | (2) Instead of a deduction in respect of the actual expenses incurred in relation to the acquisition or use of a motor vehicle, the following deductions are allowed according to the mileage covered on journeys undertaken in the assessment period for the purposes of the trade, profession or vocation—
-- src:1017 | (a) in a car, van or other motor vehicle (apart from a motorcycle), 45 pence per mile for the first 833 miles and 25 pence per mile thereafter; and
-- src:1018 | (b) on a motorcycle, 24 pence per mile,
-- src:1019 | and, if the motor vehicle is a car . . . , the only deduction allowed for the acquisition or use of that vehicle is a deduction under this paragraph.
-- src:1020 | (3) Where a person carrying on a trade, profession or vocation incurs expenses in relation to the use of accommodation occupied as their home, instead of a deduction in respect of the actual expenses, a deduction is allowed according to the number of hours spent in the assessment period on income generating activities related to the trade, profession or vocation as follows—
-- src:1021 | (a) at least 25 hours but no more than 50 hours, £10;
-- src:1022 | (b) more than 50 hours but no more than 100 hours, £18;
-- src:1023 | (c) more than 100 hours, £26.
-- src:1024 | (4) Where premises which are used by a person mainly for the purposes of a trade, profession or vocation are also occupied by that person for their personal use, whether alone or with other persons, the deduction allowed for expenses in relation to those premises is the amount that would be allowed under regulation 58(1) if the premises were used wholly and exclusively for purposes of the trade, profession or vocation, but reduced by the following amount according to the number of persons occupying the premises for their personal use—
-- src:1025 | (a) £350 for one person;
-- src:1026 | (b) £500 for two persons;
-- src:1027 | (c) £650 for three or more persons.
@ref reg 58; reg 59 (src:1001-1027)
GIVEN claimed IS AN `Expenses claimed for a trade, profession or vocation in an assessment period`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 58 and 59 — the expenses allowed for an assessment period` claimed MEANS
    `core — an amount rounded to the nearest penny`
        (   (sum (map (GIVEN payment YIELD `reg 58 — the deduction allowed for a payment` payment)
                      (filter (GIVEN payment YIELD NOT (payment's `kind of payment` EQUALS `use of premises used mainly for the trade, profession or vocation and also occupied for personal use`)) (claimed's payments))))
          PLUS (max 0 ((`reg 58 and 59 — the premises payments` claimed) MINUS (`reg 59(4) — the reduction for personal use of the premises` (claimed's `number of persons occupying the premises for their personal use`))))
          PLUS (`reg 59(2) — the deduction for mileage` (claimed's `miles covered in a car, van or other motor vehicle (apart from a motorcycle)`) (claimed's `miles covered on a motorcycle`))
          PLUS (IF claimed's `the person takes the deduction under regulation 59(3) for use of their home instead of the actual expenses`
                THEN `reg 59(3) — the deduction for use of the person's home` (claimed's `hours spent in the assessment period on income generating activities related to the trade, profession or vocation`)
                ELSE 0))
